  triage:title "crates/atm-graft-python/src/lib.rs exceeds the RULE-003 1000-line file cap after AW.4" ;
  triage:description "qa-pr1181-r1 (msg 01M1QS4C69FTKB887D5K0V12Y8) at 9f4d3170e: arch-qa RULE-003: lib.rs grew from 902 to 1096 non-test lines (+194) in this commit alone, crossing the 1000-line cap; independently re-verified by quality-mgr via mod-tests-boundary counts on both revisions. Zero-tolerance rule. Split lib.rs (e.g. extract observability_paths / ack_tool / with_daemon_recovery groupings into a submodule). CLOSURE (qa-cipher-fix, quality-mgr): Cipher's 33a03603d extracted DaemonRecoveryPolicy::strategy, PyGraftSession::recovery_endpoint_kind, with_daemon_recovery, and its recover_daemon_unavailable/recovery_attempt/recovery_outcome helpers plus RecoveryContext into a new crates/atm-graft-python/src/recovery.rs (183 lines), a mechanical move (identical bodies, forwards via pub(super) and super:: paths, no logic changes). quality-mgr independently ran .just/check_line_counts.py: lib.rs production line count now 800 (was 1096), workspace-wide RULE-003 check passes. cargo check -p atm-graft-python compiles clean at 33a03603d. Finding closed." ;
